    "category": "Professional Programming",
    "tags": [
      "Panels",
      "Professional Programming"
    ],
    "description": "The Comedy industry is ever-changing and the historic mechanisms that once anointed comedians no longer exists. It’s not a network, it’s not a Late Night set, nor a festival. Modern comedians need to be everything from marketing specialists, media talent, podcasters and business owners in addition to just being funny to make it. This panel of club owners, comedians, managers, and marketing pros will have a frank discussion about how they are constructing the careers of tomorrow’s superstars.\n\nThis River Pavilion panel is open to Pro and Industry (Artist Alley, Writers Block, Press, Content Creator, Panelist, Exhibitor, and Sidekick) ticket holders only.",
