    "description": "The Muppets returned to the big screen in 2011 with a heartfelt, music-filled celebration of friendship, found family and putting on one more show. Before the screening, Matt Vogel (Kermit the Frog, Floyd Pepper and Uncle Deadly), Eric Jacobson (Miss Piggy, Fozzie Bear and Animal), Dave Goelz (Gonzo, Dr. Bunsen Honeydew and Waldorf), Bill Barretta (Pepe the King Prawn, Rowlf the Dog and the Swedish Chef) and legendary Muppet designer Bonnie Erickson (Miss Piggy, Statler and Waldorf) discuss the craft, collaboration and creativity behind bringing these beloved characters to life—and the enduring magic of The Muppets.\n\nAll tickets are based on order of admittance into the NYCC Main Stage with Third Entry Seating Ticket holders being the last to be admitted.\n\n7:00PM - Doors to the Event open to ticket holders. In order to guarantee a spot in your designated tier you must be in line by this time.\n\n7:30PM – Event begins.\n\nThere are enough seats for everyone, but anyone arriving after their designated entrance time runs the risk of losing their seating priority, so please plan accordingly.",
